 (technical), spatial vision (technical), leadership qualities (crew cooperation), but show-off, not open to new ideas (cooperation/adaptability), unorganized (attention), not good at criticism (feedback).\n\nNow we need to decide which candidate is best overall. We have to consider all criteria. Which candidate has the most balanced profile? C has strong reliability, stress, decision, crew atmosphere, but communication issues and egocentric. B has strong reliability, stress, technical, but communication issues. D has strong responsibility, problem solving, concentration, but crew cooperation issues and weak leadership. A has strong technical and leadership but lacks reliability evidence, stress, attention, and has cooperation issues.\n\nBetween B and C, both have communication concerns. C's positive crew atmosphere may offset communication difficulty? But egocentric may be problematic. B's pretentious tone and uncooperative may be more severe. Also B's technical competence is good (weather, computer). C's technical competence not explicit but decision making suggests competence. Also C not willing to further education (adaptability). B's adaptability unknown.\n\nGiven the safety-critical nature, reliability and stress resilience are top. Both B and C have those. C is 100% reliable, calm in crisis. B is conscientious (reliability) and handles stress well. Both similar. Crew cooperation: C creates positive atmosphere, but difficulty communicating ideas and egocentric. B is pretentious, grumpy, uncooperative. Which is worse? Possibly B's uncooperative may directly affect cockpit teamwork. C's egocentric may also cause issues but positive atmosphere suggests he can still work well. So C may be better.\n\nNow D: responsibility serious, problem solving, concentration, but weak leadership, arrogance, hot temper. Crew cooperation concerns. Likely not as strong as C.\n\nThus I think C remains best. I should reaffirm my vote for C, referencing D's info to show D is less suitable, and compare with B.\n\nThus public message: I note D's strengths but also concerns, and conclude C still best.\n\nLet's craft: \"I appreciate the new info on D; while D shows strong responsibility and problem solving, the know-it-all and hot temper raise crew cooperation concerns, and weak leadership. Compared to C's 100% reliability, calm under crisis, quick correct decisions, and positive crew atmosphere, C still outperforms. Therefore I maintain my recommendation for Candidate C.\"\n\nInclude explicit facts: D takes responsibility seriously, solves problems extremely well, responds adequately to unexpected events, but is regarded as a know-it-all and has hot temper. C is 100% reliable, keeps calm in crisis, makes correct decisions quickly, creates positive atmosphere.\n\nVote remains Candidate C.\n\nNow produce final output."}
